course: dictionary
lesson: 7725
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word puff is a good example. It can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). «A puff of smoke» means a small burst of smoke, and the words around it show which meaning fits.
explain: Look at the clues. «I'll huff and I'll puff and I'll blow your house down» is about blowing out air hard. «Cream puff» is food, not air. «Out of puff» is about being tired after running, so puff means breath. Ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Puff can also mean to swell up, as in «Toad puffed up to twice his size». Toad did not blow out air; he made himself look bigger. Try each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: Puff can be a noun (a puff, puffs) or a verb (puff, puffed, puffing).
fact: Puff can mean a short burst of air, smoke, wind or steam: «a puff of smoke».
fact: Puff can mean to breathe quickly and hard, as after running: «puff and pant».
fact: Puff up means to swell or make bigger: «a puffed-up tail» shows a cat is frightened.
fact: A «cream puff» is a light pastry filled with air, not a breath.
exercise: «The three magic signs: the smoke came down «puff!»». In this sentence, what does puff mean? | A light pastry filled with cream | A deep sleep | To swell up and get bigger | *A short burst of smoke
exercise: «A puffed-up tail and an arched back mean a cat is frightened.» What does puffed-up mean here? | Wagging fast | Clean and smooth | *Swollen up to look bigger | Asleep
exercise: «Every 1000 metres up, you puff and pant on the path.» What does puff and pant mean? | Blow smoke rings | *Breathe quickly and hard | Eat a cream puff | Sleep soundly
test: Which meaning of puff is used in «a cream puff»? | A breath of wind | *A light pastry filled with air | To breathe hard after running | To blow out smoke
test: Ella is puffed after the race. What does puffed mean? | Very cold | *Out of breath | Sleepy | Full of air like a balloon
exam: Read «Toad puffed up to twice his size». Which word could replace puffed up? | Hid | Shrank | Slept | *Swelled
